Description: CVE-2026-59869 - js-yaml merge (<<) key amplification denial of service.
 Chained merge aliases (e.g. a1 merges a0, a2 merges a1, ...) let a small YAML
 document expand into an enormous number of key-copy operations during load,
 consuming CPU/time superlinearly (advisory GHSA-52cp-r559-cp3m). This backport
 introduces a `maxTotalMergeKeys` loader option (default 10000) that caps the
 total number of keys processed by merge across a single load()/loadAll() call
 and throws a YAMLException once the cap is exceeded. Set to -1 to disable.
 Backport of upstream 59423c6f (semantics) hand-ported to the v4.0.0 ES5 loader.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/59423c6f8cdc78742ac00e25a4dd39ef16b702e4
Origin: backport, https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml/commit/24f13e79ee1343a7e30bd6f6c9d9cdbf0ac9b2b7
